QQ-1  CONTROL-ONLY CALIBRATION: what depth-based detection would do to the criterion
==========================================================================================
  C1 and C2 are NOT touched. Controls only, the four declared in the plan.

--- the detector OO-1 actually used: absolute cutoffs ---
region                          <90          <110          <125          <140          <155          <170          <185
ctrl (900,150)           67/2          67/1          60/5          57/5          63/5          68/4          63/6      
ctrl (1100,430)          15/0          12/2           8/0           4/2           4/0           2/0           2/0      
ctrl (150,150)            2/0           0/0           4/0          19/0          13/0           9/1           5/0      
ctrl (1150,800)           9/0          17/0          17/0           8/1           9/0           8/0           4/0      
MAX  sized/X-sig               67/2          67/2          60/5          57/5          63/5          68/4          63/6

--- the detector QQ-1 forbids: depth below a 41px local median ---
region                         >=10          >=15          >=19          >=25          >=30          >=39
ctrl (900,150)           71/6          74/9          82/11         87/9          92/8          97/6      
ctrl (1100,430)          16/2          12/2          12/1          13/2          15/3          17/3      
ctrl (150,150)           13/1          13/1          18/0          16/0          18/0          20/0      
ctrl (1150,800)          45/2          44/2          45/1          41/0          29/4          21/2      
MAX  sized/X-sig               71/6          74/9         82/11          87/9          92/8          97/6

--- WHAT IS MEASURED ---
  worst-case control, absolute cutoffs :    68 sized components,   6 X-signatures
  worst-case control, depth detection  :    97 sized components,  11 X-signatures
  components   x1.4      X-signatures x1.8

  So depth detection roughly DOUBLES the control's false-positive bound, 6 -> 11.
  It does NOT explode it. The brief's premise that the controls 'would fire far
  more' is measured here as x1.8, which is an increase and not a blowout.

--- AND THE BRIEF'S STATED REASON DOES NOT FOLLOW FROM IT ---
  By the asymmetric-void rule the same brief asks to be written down, an
  OVER-firing control plus a region that finds nothing means absence MAY be
  claimed. A detector that fires MORE on controls therefore makes an absence
  argument STRONGER, not weaker -- provided the region still finds nothing.

  What made block B (1.14) void in the BLOCKING sense was not that its controls
  over-fired. It was that R1's own counts, 13-17, sat INSIDE the control range
  at a bar of 14. The blocking condition is the REGION's count being
  indistinguishable from the control's -- not the control's level by itself.

  At absolute cutoffs the circles returned 0-1 against controls of 0-6: far
  below, so absence is claimable. At depth the circles are UNMEASURED, so which
  side of the asymmetry a depth run would land on CANNOT be stated from these
  numbers. It would depend on what the circles returned.

--- THE REASONS NOT TO RE-RUN THAT DO HOLD ---
  1. THE TOPOLOGY LIMIT, which is decisive and is independent of any count.
     The criterion requires EXACTLY ONE 4-WAY JUNCTION. REPORT 6 records that at
     sub-pixel stroke widths 'strokes that narrow merge, so a junction and a
     near-miss render identically'. Depth detection at 10-19 levels operates
     precisely where strokes are sub-pixel, so the feature the criterion tests
     for stops being distinguishable from its own negation. The instrument is
     wrong there whatever the control counts say.
  2. CHANGING THE INSTRUMENT AFTER SEEING THE RESULT needs fresh pre-registration.
     OO-1 was pre-registered at absolute cutoffs 90-185. Swapping detectors now
     is the STOP_R10_SET_C problem and PP-3's forking paths in one move.

  CONCLUSION: do not re-run -- on reasons 1 and 2, not on the control counts.
  And the OO-1 negative is SCOPED TO CONTRAST either way: it excludes a pair of
  X marks at ordinary pen contrast and has UNMEASURED sensitivity below the floor.
